{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>To the many you shall increase his inheritance.</b> To a tribe that was numerous in population they gave a large portion. And even though the portions were not equal — since they divided the portions all according to the multitude of the tribe — they did so only by lot, and the lot was by the holy spirit, as is explained in Bava Batra (122a): Elazar the kohen would be clothed in Urim and Tumim and would say by the holy spirit: if such-and-such tribe comes up, such-and-such territory comes up with it. And the tribes were written on twelve slips and twelve territories on twelve slips, and they mixed them in the box, and the prince would put his hand inside and take out two slips. There would come up in his hand the slip of his tribe's name and the slip of the territory designated for him. And the lot itself would cry out and say: I, the lot, have come up for the territory of such-and-such, for the tribe of such-and-such, as it is said: ״עַל פִּי הַגּוֹרָל״ (according to the lot). And the land was not divided by measure, because one territory is better than another, but by valuation: a kor of poor land against a se'ah of good land — all according to the value."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:57.522246777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}